.Dd November 8, 2026
.Dt MK.SEARCHPATHS.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.searchpaths.mk
.Nd where a module finds headers and libraries
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Gives a program or library module its include paths and its library search path:
the module's own
.Pa include/ ,
its framework's
.Pa include/
and
.Pa local/include/ ,
and those of every framework named in
.Va PREREQS
of its framework, then the library files
.Va LIBS
names.
Not included directly by a makefile:
.Xr mk.prog.mk 5
and
.Xr mk.lib.mk 5
read it after they know their framework's directory.
.Pp
A path in a command, such as an
.Fl I ,
an
.Fl L
or a run path, is written for the shell: a directory with a space, a parenthesis,
an apostrophe, an ampersand or a hash sign in its name is quoted.
A path that make has to read in a dependency line, such as a header the compiler
lists in a dependency file or a library a relink waits for, is another matter:
make cannot write a space or a parenthesis there.
Those paths are therefore relative to the module directory, which is where
.Xr bmake 1
always runs, so no part of the workspace's path is in them.
A prerequisite framework whose name has a space or a parenthesis in it, or that
lives in a
.Va PARENT_WS
directory whose path has one, is reached through a link in the module's own build
directory,
.Pa build/ Ns Ar key Ns Pa /prereqs/ Ns Ar name ,
named with the name's encoded form (see
.Xr mk.common.mk 5 ) ,
which has neither.
The links are made when the module is built, before anything is compiled.
.Pp
Library files are looked up in the module's framework first, then in the
prerequisite frameworks, in the order of
.Va PREREQS .
.Sh TARGETS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm _create_prereq_links
Makes the links above.
A prerequisite of the module's
.Cm all
target.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mk.common.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.framework.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.lib.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.prog.mk 5 ,
.Xr bmake-it 7
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Sylvain Souche
